of an account number are ever shown; an Admin confirms new details with you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Next time, sign in at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/sign-in</span> with your Email and Password, then <b class="gd-ui">Sign in</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Link expired? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send me a new link</b> on the page it opens, or ask an Admin for a password link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in with your phone: on <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b> and enter the 6-digit code we text you. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Use my phone number instead</b> on the sign-in page. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/645"><img src="/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="645"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.4%;top:78.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Recommended: open your profile and press <b class="gd-ui">Set up two-step sign-in</b>. Scan the code with your authenticator app, type the 6 digits and press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>. After that every sign-in asks for a code.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-stuck-on-a-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stuck on a page?</h2><p class="gd-p">If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks <b class="gd-ui">Need a hand with</b> the page. <b class="gd-ui">Open the guide section</b> opens this guide at the chapter for that page beside it (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); <b class="gd-ui">Back to what I was doing</b> closes it and everything you typed is still there. <b class="gd-ui">Open the Academy lesson</b> opens the lesson in a new tab. <b class="gd-ui">Not now</b> quiets it on that page for a day.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'academy', 'chapter', 'commissions', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. If the academy gate is on, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths; the guide and your profile stay open.', 'Academy', 'Your training path: lessons narrated by your browser, a quiz per section, 80% to pass.',
